      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# H3 Scene Retake\n\nOne scene of a finished run did not land? Render **just that scene again** - no writer, no other scenes.\n\n1. **`bundle`** = *latest* is the newest saved run in `output/apnext_scenes/` (every writer saves one with `save_scenes` on); pick a specific file for an older run.\n2. Set **`scene_number`**, optionally paste and edit the scene into **`prompt_override`** (empty = the bundle's prompt).\n3. Click **🎬 Retake this scene** - it bumps the seed and queues ONLY this node (the model loaders are cached). Each click is a new take; the Prompt Preview below shows the prompt it rendered.\n4. **Continuity:** if the run was chain-rendered with `save_latents` on, the previous scene's saved take (`output/apnext_latents/<project>_sNN.pt`) is pinned to the head - picture and sound - with `context_frames` / `context_mode` set to what the chain render used. No saved take = hard cut.\n5. **Music videos:** connect a Load Audio with the song to `master_audio`; the scene's piece is cut at the bundle's segment and masked in. **Films:** leave it unconnected. Wire the same `ref_image` pictures the run used.\n\nThe clip lands at `filename_prefix` + `_sNN_retake`; swap it into your join. Models, sampler and resolution are the short-film setup - change them to match the run you are retaking."
      ],
      "title": "How this works",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
